From 4c5cb692f3870f56b80e56374cd2e044051dc9ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 02:48:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] WIP refinement: the libc models' heap
 (__prism_alloc/__prism_free), nondet values and assumptions; loop-cut docs
 and parity tests

Lean: SInst nondet / vassume / halloc / hfree with strict and LangRef-side
semantics, translation, simulation (freeChk_run: MemTr::dealloc's checks fail
exactly on freeBad) and lazy lifting. C++: the hidden allocation-failed flag
object is preassigned (variable after the entry globals', object after theirs
in the prologue) when the analysed function can reach __prism_alloc_failed
(pirmem::reaches_alloc_failed, shared with the exporter); the exporter inlines
library models and other-file callees (no C signed shift there), threads the
flag object to them as an extra argument, and writes the model intrinsics.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PNtqaD75q6kS9GMoczxQVx
